# 🔑 InfinityAI.Pro Required API Keys & Credentials

## 📋 Complete Credentials Checklist

Before running the deployment scripts, gather these credentials:

---

## 1. ☁️ **Azure AI (Primary Provider)**

### Azure OpenAI Service
- **Service**: Azure OpenAI
- **Purpose**: Primary LLM (GPT-4 Turbo)
- **Portal**: [Azure Portal](https://portal.azure.com)
- **Steps**:
  1. Create "Azure OpenAI" resource
  2. Deploy GPT-4 model
  3. Get endpoint and keys
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - `AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT` - Your Azure OpenAI resource endpoint
  - `AZURE_OPENAI_KEY` - Primary API key
  - `AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT` - Model deployment name (usually "gpt-4-turbo")

### Azure Speech Services
- **Service**: Cognitive Services - Speech
- **Purpose**: Real-time speech transcription
- **Portal**: [Azure Portal](https://portal.azure.com)
- **Steps**:
  1. Create "Cognitive Services" resource
  2. Enable Speech service
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - `AZURE_SPEECH_ENDPOINT` - Speech service endpoint
  - `AZURE_SPEECH_KEY` - Speech API key

### Azure Vision Services
- **Service**: Cognitive Services - Vision
- **Purpose**: Advanced image analysis
- **Portal**: [Azure Portal](https://portal.azure.com)
- **Steps**:
  1. Create "Cognitive Services" resource
  2. Enable Vision service
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - `AZURE_VISION_ENDPOINT` - Vision service endpoint
  - `AZURE_VISION_KEY` - Vision API key

### Azure Text Analytics
- **Service**: Cognitive Services - Text Analytics
- **Purpose**: Sentiment analysis
- **Portal**: [Azure Portal](https://portal.azure.com)
- **Steps**:
  1. Create "Cognitive Services" resource
  2. Enable Text Analytics service
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - `AZURE_TEXT_ANALYTICS_ENDPOINT` - Text Analytics endpoint
  - `AZURE_TEXT_ANALYTICS_KEY` - Text Analytics API key

### Azure ML (Optional - for advanced signal generation)
- **Service**: Azure Machine Learning
- **Purpose**: Cloud ML model hosting
- **Portal**: [Azure Portal](https://portal.azure.com)
- **Steps**:
  1. Create "Machine Learning" workspace
  2. Deploy models (optional)
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - `AZURE_ML_ENDPOINT` - ML workspace endpoint
  - `AZURE_ML_KEY` - ML workspace key

---

## 2. ☁️ **AWS AI (Secondary Provider)**

### AWS Account Setup
- **Service**: AWS IAM
- **Purpose**: Cloud access and billing
- **Portal**: [AWS Console](https://console.aws.amazon.com)
- **Steps**:
  1. Create AWS account
  2. Set up billing alerts
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` - IAM user access key
  - `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` - IAM user secret key
  - `AWS_REGION` - Region (recommended: us-east-1)

### AWS Bedrock (Secondary LLM)
- **Service**: Amazon Bedrock
- **Purpose**: Fallback LLM (Claude 3.5)
- **Portal**: [AWS Bedrock Console](https://console.aws.amazon.com/bedrock)
- **Steps**:
  1. Enable Amazon Bedrock
  2. Request access to Claude models
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - Uses same AWS credentials above
  - `AWS_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` - Model ID (anthropic.claude-3-5-sonnet-20240620-v1:0)

### AWS S3 (Model Storage)
- **Service**: Amazon S3
- **Purpose**: AI model storage
- **Portal**: [AWS S3 Console](https://console.aws.amazon.com/s3)
- **Steps**:
  1. Create bucket named "infinityai-models"
  2. Set public read permissions for models/
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - `AWS_S3_BUCKET` - Bucket name (infinityai-models)
  - Uses same AWS credentials

### AWS SageMaker (Optional - Advanced ML)
- **Service**: Amazon SageMaker
- **Purpose**: ML model training/deployment
- **Portal**: [AWS SageMaker Console](https://console.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker)
- **Steps**:
  1. Create SageMaker domain
  2. Set up notebook instances
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - `AWS_SAGEMAKER_ENDPOINT` - SageMaker endpoint URL

---

## 3. 🤗 **Hugging Face**

### Hugging Face Account
- **Service**: Hugging Face Hub
- **Purpose**: Local AI models and tokenization
- **Portal**: [Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co)
- **Steps**:
  1. Create free account
  2. Generate API token
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - `HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY` - API token from settings

---

## 4. 🏦 **Broker Integration**

### Dhan (Primary Broker)
- **Service**: Dhan HQ
- **Purpose**: Live trading execution
- **Portal**: [Dhan HQ](https://dhan.co)
- **Steps**:
  1. Create trading account
  2. Generate API credentials
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - `DHAN_ACCESS_TOKEN` - API access token
  - `DHAN_CLIENT_ID` - Client ID
- **Optional**:
  - `BROKER_TYPE` - Set to "dhan"

### CoinSwitch Pro (Alternative Broker)
- **Service**: CoinSwitch Pro
- **Purpose**: Alternative trading execution
- **Portal**: [CoinSwitch Pro](https://coinswitch.co)
- **Steps**:
  1. Create trading account
  2. Generate API credentials
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - `COINSWITCH_API_KEY` - API key
  - `COINSWITCH_API_SECRET` - API secret
- **Optional**:
  - `BROKER_TYPE` - Set to "coinswitch"

---

## 5. 🐙 **GitHub (Deployment)**

### GitHub Repository
- **Service**: GitHub
- **Purpose**: Code hosting and Render deployment
- **Portal**: [GitHub](https://github.com)
- **Steps**:
  1. Create repository named "InfinityAI.Pro"
  2. Push code to main branch
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - Repository URL (automatically detected by scripts)

---

## 6. 🎨 **Optional External APIs**

### OpenAI (Fallback)
- **Service**: OpenAI API
- **Purpose**: Emergency LLM fallback
- **Portal**: [OpenAI](https://platform.openai.com)
- **Steps**:
  1. Create account
  2. Add credits
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - `OPENAI_API_KEY` - OpenAI API key

### Perplexity AI (Research)
- **Service**: Perplexity AI
- **Purpose**: Market research and news
- **Portal**: [Perplexity AI](https://www.perplexity.ai)
- **Steps**:
  1. Create account
  2. Generate API key
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - `PERPLEXITY_API_KEY` - Perplexity API key

### TradingView (Charts)
- **Service**: TradingView
- **Purpose**: Technical analysis
- **Portal**: [TradingView](https://www.tradingview.com)
- **Steps**:
  1. Create account
  2. Generate API key
- **Credentials Needed**:
  - `TRADINGVIEW_API_KEY` - TradingView API key

---

## 💰 **Cost Estimates**

### Monthly Budget Planning:
- **Azure AI**: $50-200 (GPT-4, Vision, Speech)
- **AWS AI**: $30-150 (Bedrock, S3, other services)
- **Hugging Face**: Free (with API limits)
- **Render Hosting**: $7-50 (depending on usage)
- **Broker**: Variable (trading commissions)
- **Total**: $87-400/month

### Free Tiers Available:
- Hugging Face: Unlimited free API calls
- Azure: $200 credit for new accounts
- AWS: Free tier for 12 months
- Render: 750 hours free/month

---

## 🔧 **Quick Setup Checklist**

### Before Running Scripts:
- [ ] Azure account with OpenAI service
- [ ] AWS account with Bedrock access
- [ ] Hugging Face account and token
- [ ] Broker account (Dhan or CoinSwitch)
- [ ] GitHub repository created
- [ ] Budget alerts set up

### Priority Order:
1. **Azure OpenAI** (Primary AI)
2. **AWS Account** (Secondary AI + Storage)
3. **Hugging Face** (Local models)
4. **Broker Account** (Trading)
5. **GitHub** (Deployment)

---

## 🚀 **Next Steps**

Once you have these credentials:

1. **Run the setup script**:
   ```bash
   ./setup_env_vars.sh
   ```

2. **Choose option 1** for interactive setup

3. **Enter credentials** when prompted (keys are hidden)

4. **Copy the generated variables** to Render dashboard

5. **Deploy and verify**:
   ```bash
   ./deploy_complete.sh
   ```

---

## 🆘 **Getting Help**

If you need assistance with any service:

- **Azure**: Check [Azure Documentation](https://docs.microsoft.com/azure)
- **AWS**: Use [AWS Getting Started](https://aws.amazon.com/getting-started)
- **Hugging Face**: See [Hugging Face Docs](https://huggingface.co/docs)
- **Render**: Visit [Render Docs](https://docs.render.com)

